From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: IamMaxim <g.maxim.stepanoff@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 10 Jun 2026 01:12:54 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] feature: install prebuilt extensions from a local path
 (air-gapped)

Add ExtensionStore::install_prebuilt_extension(source): installs a prebuilt
extension from a local directory or .tar.gz archive with no network and no
compilation, reusing the existing toolchain-free load path. Refuses (bails) if
the input ships Rust source but no compiled extension.wasm, pointing the user to
build it on a networked machine. Reuses the existing async-compression/async-tar
deps for unpack; no http_client/URL path is reintroduced.

Test covers both the directory and .tar.gz install paths (RealFs + TempTree),
asserting the extension installs as a real (dev:false) extension and its theme
registers.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
